# Titan: keep the vendor's configstore HAL from starting, added by 65-extra-init.
#
# android.hardware.configstore@1.1-service from the Titan's Android 10 vendor
# runs under that release's seccomp policy, and Android 16's libc makes a system
# call the policy does not allow: the service is killed with SIGSYS as it
# starts, init restarts it, and it dies again - every 5 s for as long as the
# phone is on (12 Nov 2026: hundreds of core dumps in one boot, each one a
# systemd-coredump run and with it a network namespace torn down, which also
# filled the kernel log with retire_sysctl_set warnings). Nothing on Android 16
# asks configstore for anything: surfaceflinger reads system properties since
# Android 12.
#
# Same definition as the vendor's, plus override and disabled; this file sorts
# after android.hardware.configstore@1.1-service.rc, so init reads it last.
# The Titan's deviceinfo also lists the service in
# deviceinfo_android_skip_services, or start-android-hals.sh would start it
# because it is disabled.
service vendor.configstore-hal /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.configstore@1.1-service
    override
    class hal animation
    user system
    group system
    disabled
